Z||000000||GTsaint||09-17-1999||01:17 AM||||<BR>I have a 87 GT and ever since i accidently ran out of gas (the gauge was wrong), my GT stalls on the first time on a cold start.  Then i restart it and it runs fine.<P>When i ran out of gas and cranked it to try and start, but it didnt, did i put air in the gas line? Do i have to purge the line or represserize the system?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Patrick||09-17-1999||02:27 AM||||<BR>This is just a suggestion, but when you ran low on fuel it might be possible that you sucked some crap from the bottom of your gas tank into the fuel filter.<P>If your filter was doing it's job, just changing the filter might rectify your problem. If the filter wasn't doing it's job, well, I hate to think what might be gummed up now, ie. injectors.<P>||||reg||3
Z||000002||GTsaint||09-17-1999||11:41 AM||||Is it easy to change a fuel filter on a Fiero like it is on older cars?  Anything special i have to do?||||reg||1
Z||000003||AL||09-17-1999||08:08 PM||||well, put  jack under the passenger side rear, lift it up, get on your back and it's right ther, it lookslike a little can. unscrew it off, a little gas might come out, put the new one in and presto your done. also put on safety glasses on so gas won't hit your eyes. ||||reg||6
